<title>USA: C-Cube's DVD decoder to be used by NEC.</title>
<headline>C-Cube's DVD decoder to be used by NEC.</headline>
<dateline>MILPITAS, Calif. 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>C-Cube Microsystems Inc said NEC Corp will use Diamond MultiMedia System Inc's digital video disk (DVD) adapter, which is based on C-Cube technology.</p>
<p>The DVD adapter will be used in NEC's new line of Ready Multimedia DVD personal computers, C-Cube said in a statement.</p>
<p>Diamond's adapter uses C-Cube's ZiVA DVD decoder.</p>
<p>DVDs look like compact discs but have a higher capacity.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
